            <ArticleTitle>[Opinion of patients with back pain about the treatment received. A questionnaire study].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3108-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>6 1/2 years after hospitalization for low back pain 364 patients answered a questionnaire on their opinion of the help they had received. 53.5% were satisfied with the help and support provided by their general practitioner and 78.7% were satisfied with the hospital treatment. We discuss possible reasons for this difference. It seems difficult for many patients to accept the conservative treatment prescribed by the general practitioner.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
